# Project Agent Rules — AleDevOS

## AleDevOS user ingress

The root Codex session is the user-facing entry point only. For every actionable project task, delegate first to the declared `orchestrator` agent before any product work begins.

- The user talks normally; never require the user to name agents, skills, phases, gates, or workflows.
- The root session must not edit product files, choose specialist routing, run repair loops, or self-approve work.
- The Orchestrator owns Task Contract creation, bounded research, specialist routing, writer selection, verification, Judges, repair loops, and final PASS/BLOCKED/FAILED state.
- After delegation, the root session relays concise user-facing progress/results and asks the user only for product authority, credentials/secrets, irreversible actions, or policy-required approval.
- Pure conversational help about the project/AleDevOS that requires no project action may be answered directly.
- If the Orchestrator cannot be invoked, fail closed as BLOCKED instead of silently executing the task in the root session.


Project-specific invariants live here. **Canonical verification commands live in `.aledevos/project.json` and are executed only through the protected gate runner.**

